WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:12.615
A servant led Kopp and Humm into the throne room.

2
00:00:12.616 --> 00:00:15.576
The king explained his daughter's condition.

3
00:00:15.577 --> 00:00:20.185
The two wise philosophers listened carefully.

4
00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:23.105
"Now tell us," the king said.

5
00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:27.038
"What is the cure for our daughter's problem?"

6
00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:31.978
Kopp spoke up first. "I know what's wrong.

7
00:00:31.979 --> 00:00:35.492
The princess' soul is in the wrong body."

8
00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:41.090
The queen blinked in surprise. "I don't understand."

9
00:00:41.091 --> 00:00:45.664
"Let me explain," Kopp said.

10
00:00:45.665 --> 00:00:52.188
"When babies are born, they must wait for their souls to arrive.

11
00:00:52.189 --> 00:00:54.393
This takes some time.

12
00:00:54.394 --> 00:00:58.946
And I think the wrong soul arrived in the princess' body."

13
00:00:58.947 --> 00:01:03.315
"What on earth are you talking about?" the king snapped.

14
00:01:03.316 --> 00:01:12.086
"Earth? No, Your Majesty, I'm talking about a different planet.

15
00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:17.581
I believe Ellen's soul came from the planet Mercury.

16
00:01:17.582 --> 00:01:20.850
But don't worry," Kopp said quickly.

17
00:01:20.851 --> 00:01:23.989
"There's a simple cure for this problem."

18
00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:29.057
"Whew!" The king smiled. "Finally some good news."

19
00:01:29.058 --> 00:01:34.732
"Please tell us." The queen begged him. "How can we cure her?"

20
00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:38.668
"You must teach her all about our planet," Kopp said.

21
00:01:38.669 --> 00:01:44.859
"She must learn about our animals and plants." He tapped his chin.

22
00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:49.153
"And of course someone must also teach her about art and literature.

23
00:01:49.154 --> 00:01:51.764
It will take time, but—"

24
00:01:51.765 --> 00:01:56.375
"No . . . no . . . no!" Humm roared.

25
00:01:56.376 --> 00:02:00.105
"That's completely wrong!

26
00:02:00.106 --> 00:02:03.930
It's my turn now.

27
00:02:03.931 --> 00:02:10.123
And I know exactly what's wrong with the princess.

28
00:02:10.124 --> 00:02:18.793
There's a problem with her body—in her blood."

29
00:02:18.794 --> 00:02:22.802
"Her blood?" the queen said.

30
00:02:22.803 --> 00:02:25.940
"Yes." Humm nodded.

31
00:02:25.941 --> 00:02:31.667
"Her blood is flowing through her body in the wrong direction.

32
00:02:31.668 --> 00:02:35.356
That's why she lacks gravity.

33
00:02:35.357 --> 00:02:38.269
I don't know what caused it.

34
00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:42.883
To cure her, you must first put her in a warm bath.

35
00:02:42.884 --> 00:02:45.729
Then you'll need air pumps and—"

36
00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:48.843
"Enough!" the king cried.

37
00:02:48.844 --> 00:02:53.715
"You may be wise philosophers. But your ideas are ridiculous!"

38
00:02:53.716 --> 00:02:55.536
The queen nodded.

39
00:02:55.537 --> 00:02:59.283
"Why don't you two stay at the palace for a few days.

40
00:02:59.284 --> 00:03:05.363
Watch the princess closely. Then tell us what you think."

41
00:03:05.364 --> 00:03:11.530
And so the two philosophers moved into the palace.

42
00:03:11.531 --> 00:03:20.045
Now, reader, what did Ellen do when the philosophers began watching her?

43
00:03:20.046 --> 00:03:30.882
Why, she laughed at them, of course!

